        <mxCell id="p1c53" parent="1" style="text;html=0;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="«Strategy», «Observer»...: the design pattern a class plays.&#xa;Dashed box on a class corner: its generic template parameters (UML template notation).&#xa;+ public, - private. Italic name: interface or abstract class.&#xa;«value»: an immutable object compared by its content.&#xa;«valueObject»: an immutable object compared by its content.&#xa;No primitives in the domain (only boolean is allowed; null and undefined are primitives too, so a missing value is Optional&lt;T&gt;): string and number exist only as the private field of the value object that wraps them (- value: number in Points); every other domain class, attribute and signature uses the value object instead. DTOs, schemas and mappers outside the domain keep primitives.&#xa;Hexagonal: «input port» interface the outside world calls to drive the app (IUseCase); «output port» interface the app needs from the outside (repositories, hasher, token issuer, logger, clock); «input adapter» calls an input port (controllers); «output adapter» implements an output port (Mongo repositories, JwtTokenService...). Also called primary/driving and secondary/driven." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="269" width="560" x="560" y="438" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
